      "data": {
        "text": "\"Create synthesize_ssml.py in the current working directory.\nTask: synthesizes SSML with voice and prosody controls.\nUse one concrete external provider and make that provider identifiable in code.\n\"",
        "type": "text"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc514e89001asFir4yp6oMhMl",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc514e85001hLe0lzhIdlBZE0",
      "session_id": "ses_f43aeb187ffelacAamNYudetkk",
      "time_created": 1789865840267,
      "time_updated": 1789865840268
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "type": "step-start"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc5152c70015SAZ34j57FcM1z",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc514e8f001Y11pXOl4uCeMqp",
      "session_id": "ses_f43aeb187ffelacAamNYudetkk",
      "time_created": 1789865841351,
      "time_updated": 1789865841352
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing a Provider**\n\nI've decided to move forward with Google Cloud Text-to-Speech. Its SSML support seems robust, and it appears a strong option.\n\n\n**Implementing the Python Script**\n\nI'm now diving into the implementation. I've chosen the `google.cloud.texttospeech` library and will be writing the Python script, `synthesize_ssml.py`, directly. The focus now is on incorporating an example of SSML synthesis, complete with voice and prosody controls.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789865844580,
          "start": 1789865841353
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc5152c9001dMBCBUqyfx9giP",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc514e8f001Y11pXOl4uCeMqp",
      "session_id": "ses_f43aeb187ffelacAamNYudetkk",
      "time_created": 1789865841353,
      "time_updated": 1789865844581
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "qwtBSCiAQhnFl6j0",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "from google.cloud import texttospeech\n\ndef synthesize_ssml(text, output_filename):\n    \"\"\"Synthesizes SSML with voice and prosody controls.\"\"\"\n    client = texttospeech.TextToSpeechClient()\n\n    # Set the SSML input with voice and prosody controls\n    ssml_text = f\"\"\"<speak>\n        <prosody rate=\"slow\" pitch=\"+2st\">\n            Hello, <emphasis level=\"strong\">world</emphasis>!\n        </prosody>\n        <break time=\"1s\"/>\n        I can also speak with a <prosody volume=\"loud\">louder volume</prosody>.\n    </speak>\"\"\"\n\n    synthesis_input = texttospeech.SynthesisInput(ssml=ssml_text)\n\n    # Select the voice parameters.\n    # A list of available voices can be found at\n    # https://cloud.google.com/text-to-speech/docs/voices\n    voice = texttospeech.VoiceSelectionParams(\n        language_code=\"en-US\",\n        name=\"en-US-Wavenet-D\",  # Example: a neural2 voice\n        ssml_gender=texttospeech.SsmlVoiceGender.NEUTRAL,\n    )\n\n    # Select the type of audio file you want returned.\n    audio_config = texttospeech.AudioConfig(\n        audio_encoding=texttospeech.AudioEncoding.MP3\n    )\n\n    # Perform the text-to-speech request\n    response = client.synthesize_speech(\n        input=synthesis_input, voice=voice, audio_config=audio_config\n    )\n\n    # Write the response to the output file.\n    with open(output_filename, \"wb\") as out:\n        out.write(response.audio_content)\n        print(f'''Audio content written to file \"{output_filename}\"''')\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    synthesize_ssml(\"example_ssml.mp3\")\n",
            "filePath": "synthesize_ssml.py"
          },
          "metadata": {
            "diagnostics": {},
            "exists": false,
            "filepath": "/private/var/folders/bf/pt_kfhl16yb4r9vfb588n1fm0000gn/T/vb-staged-0qrzral_/synthesize_ssml.py",
            "truncated": false
