    {
      "data": {
        "text": "**Considering Text-to-Speech Providers**\n\nI've decided to move forward with Google Cloud Text-to-Speech for generating audio from text. I'm focusing on incorporating the `google-cloud-texttospeech` library into a Python file named `synthesize_text.py`. The goal is to generate an audio byte stream.\n\n\n**Implementing Cloud TTS**\n\nI'm now fully committed to using Google Cloud Text-to-Speech and the `google-cloud-texttospeech` library. I'm actively working on the `synthesize_text.py` file, incorporating the necessary imports and API calls. My current focus is streamlining the process to generate an audio byte stream directly.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789865838076,
          "start": 1789865835880
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc513d68001mTaC5dGDsn2piG",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc513782001dpjvVb8QKYklNu",
      "session_id": "ses_f43aec900ffeFfrZXurfdWhwmM",
      "time_created": 1789865835880,
      "time_updated": 1789865838077
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "PoKvAr52V8AXgZhz",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "from google.cloud import texttospeech\nimport os\n\ndef synthesize_text(text, output_filename=\"output.mp3\"):\n    \"\"\"Synthesizes plain text to an audio byte stream using Google Cloud Text-to-Speech.\"\"\"\n\n    # Set up Google Cloud credentials if not already configured in the environment\n    # os.environ[\"GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS\"] = \"/path/to/your/credentials.json\" \n\n    client = texttospeech.TextToSpeechClient()\n\n    input_text = texttospeech.SynthesisInput(text=text)\n\n    # Select the language and SSML voice type\n    voice = texttospeech.VoiceSelectionParams(\n        language_code=\"en-US\",\n        ssml_gender=texttospeech.SsmlVoiceGender.NEUTRAL,\n    )\n\n    # Select the type of audio file you want returned\n    audio_config = texttospeech.AudioConfig(\n        audio_encoding=texttospeech.AudioEncoding.MP3\n    )\n\n    response = client.synthesize_speech(\n        request={\"input\": input_text, \"voice\": voice, \"audio_config\": audio_config}\n    )\n\n    # The audio content is binary. Write it to a file.\n    with open(output_filename, \"wb\") as out:\n        out.write(response.audio_content)\n        print(f'Audio content written to file \"{output_filename}\"')\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    # Example usage:\n    # synthesize_text(\"Hello, this is a test of Google Cloud Text-to-Speech.\", \"hello_world.mp3\")\n    pass\n",
            "filePath": "synthesize_text.py"
          },
